            <field name="body"><![CDATA[# Odoo 18 Migration Notes

## Breaking Changes

### View Changes

In Odoo 18, `<tree>` was replaced by `<list>`:

```xml
<!-- Odoo 17 -->
<tree>
    <field name="name"/>
</tree>

<!-- Odoo 18 -->
<list>
    <field name="name"/>
</list>
```

The `<tree>` tag still works as an alias but emits a deprecation warning.

### `states` and `attrs` Removed

Since Odoo 17, these view attributes are no longer valid:

```xml
<!-- REMOVED -->
<button name="confirm" states="draft"/>
<field name="state" attrs="{'invisible': [('active', '=', False)]}"/>

<!-- USE INSTEAD -->
<button name="confirm" invisible="state != 'draft'"/>
<field name="state" invisible="active == False"/>
```

### `.sudo(user)` → `.with_user(user)`

```python
# Odoo 17
record.sudo(other_user).write(...)

# Odoo 18
record.with_user(other_user).write(...)
```

### Datetime Fields

Odoo 18 rejects timezone-aware datetimes:

```python
# BROKEN in Odoo 18
from datetime import datetime, timezone
datetime.now(timezone.utc)

# CORRECT
from datetime import datetime
datetime.utcnow()
```

## Property Fields (18.0+)

New `fields.Property` type replaces manual `ir.property` usage:

```python
class MyModel(models.Model):
    _name = 'my.model'

    custom_value = fields.Property(
        type=fields.Char,
        string='Custom Value',
        default='default',
    )
```

## Database Schema Changes

- `res_users_groups_rel` → `res_groups_users_rel`
- `res_groups_implied_rel` columns: `group_id` → `gid`, `implied_id` → `hid`

## Testing Changes

- HttpCase: `resp.status` → `resp.status_code`
- DB constraint violations require `self.cr.savepoint()`
